envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-step-gate-reply-accept
type: step_gate
id: reply.accept
context: lib/step-gates — the gate a reply passes before any of it is turned into files (0.39.282 N21).
intent: A reply that only says it could not do the work is a refusal, not a result — it is blocked, never "replied".
summary: >-
  Live evidence 2026-09-29: "I can't safely rebuild src/kernel/state.js because the project-specific code tools are not
  actually available" + an empty fence was passed on as a reply and state.js landed at 0 bytes.
system: nexus
tags: [step_gate, build]
source: docs/2026-09-29-nex-node-store-phasemap.spec#N21
payload:
  step: reply.accept
  on_block: drop
  checks:
    - id: reply-non-empty
      kind: non_empty
      min_chars: 1
    - id: reply-not-refusal
      kind: not_refusal
      # A refusal is a reply that says it cannot do the work AND carries no non-empty code. The phrases are matched
      # case-insensitively; extend them here, not in code.
      phrases:
        - "i can't safely"
        - "i cannot safely"
        - "i can't rebuild"
        - "i cannot rebuild"
        - "tools are not actually available"
        - "tools are not available"
        - "i don't have access to"
        - "i do not have access to"
        - "i'm unable to"
        - "i am unable to"
        - "i can't help with"
        - "i cannot help with"
        - "i can't complete"
        - "i cannot complete"
